==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ætla|lang=non}}.

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|ætlaði|ætlað}}

# to [[intend]], to [[plan]], to [[mean]] to{{jump|is|intend|s}}
#: ''Ég '''ætlaði''' ekki að særa þig.''
#:: I didn't '''mean''' to hurt you.
#: ''Hún '''ætlaði''' alltaf að passa upp á hann.''
#:: She was always '''going to''' keep an on him.
#: ''Ég '''ætla''' heim!''
#:: I'm '''going''' home!
# to be [[about to]] do something{{jump|is|be about to|s}}
#: ''Hættu þessu asninn þinn! Ég '''ætlaði''' að sitja þarna!''
#:: Stop that you idiot! I was '''going''' to sit there!
# to [[guess]], to [[think]], to [[believe]]{{jump|is|guess|is}}
#: '''''Ætli''' það ekki...''
#:: I '''guess''' so...
# {{context|subjunctive|lang=is}} to [[wonder]], to [[suppose]]
#: ''Hvað '''ætli''' forsetinn sé að gera núna?''
#:: I '''wonder''' what the president is doing now.
#: ''Átt þú ekki að vera í skólanum?'' — '''''Ætli''' það ekki.''
#:: Aren't you supposed to be at school? — I '''guess''' so.

====Derived terms====
* [[til þess er ætlast]]
